r, generated by a custom configurable command line statement; clicking a line in the diff opens VS Code.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_014_diff_view.md:22:- Add a configurable diff command template, executed by Electron in local mode, with placeholders for `rootProjectFolder`, `commit`, `branch` and selected file path.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_014_diff_view.md:30:- The diff is generated through the configured Electron command template with project and commit placeholders resolved.\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\project_tree_paths.test.ts:5:    it('creates folders only below the configured project folder', () => {\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_013_desktop_app.md:17:Electron already opens the React app in a `BrowserWindow`, loads the configured app URL, disables context isolation, and exposes a preload bridge as `window.md2Data`. The local Git path supports opening a `.git` folder, loading markdown files, creating the working folder, switching branches, committing, pushing and watching markdown changes. React detects the Electron bridge and can open a local project through `ProjectWorkspace`.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_013_desktop_app.md:22:- Keep the Electron main process responsible for window creation, native dialogs and app menu commands.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_013_desktop_app.md:33:- Starting the desktop app opens the React app in Electron using the configured app URL.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_034_github_oauth_cors_proxy.md:19:Not implemented. `GITHUB_OAUTH_PROXY_URL` is read by `github_auth_config.ts` but nothing is deployed at that URL, so web-mode login has no working path (Electron mode works today via `desktop/github_oauth_proxy.js` + preload). We have a small server available to host this.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_034_github_oauth_cors_proxy.md:36:- CORS is restricted to configured app origins; a request from an arbitrary origin is rejected.\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\project_session.test.ts:5:import { configureRemoteControlConnection, REMOTE_CONTROL_ENDPOINT_KEY, REMOTE_CONTROL_TOKEN_KEY } from './remote_control_connection'\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\project_session.test.ts:34:        loadProjectConfig: vi.fn(async () => null),\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\project_session.test.ts:40:        saveProjectConfig: vi.fn(),\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\project_session.test.ts:57:        configureRemoteControlConnection({ endpoint: 'ws://127.0.0.1:1234', token: 'token-1' })\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:1:import type { ProjectConfig, ProjectReference } from '../../data/data_types'\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:7:export class GithubProjectConfigStorage {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:18:    async loadProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference): Promise<Partial<ProjectConfig> | null> {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:23:        return JSON.parse(file.content) as Partial<ProjectConfig>\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:26:    async saveProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference, config: ProjectConfig) {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:32:                content: `${JSON.stringify(config, null, 2)}\\\\\\\\n`,\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\github_project_config_storage.ts:36:            message: 'Update MD² project config',\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:16:Full agent selection per the architecture: \\\\\\\"Set default agent from menu, or configurable on the action definition or when the action is started.\\\\\\\" Additionally