nfig_persistence.md:19:`ConfigService.saveDraft` applies values in memory and `ConfigPage` saves only the project scope through `dataService.saveProjectConfig()`. React-scoped values (`react.autoCommitDelayMs`, `react.showStartupSplash`) reset on every reload. Desktop values come from read-only env vars (`desktop/config.js` `resolveDesktopConfig`) with no writeback IPC, so editing `desktop.agent` in the UI is lost on restart — and the conversation-continue path in `preload.js` reads the env value directly, ignoring UI edits (see B-006). Two entries are dead: `react.showStartupSplash` and `connection.githubScopes` are editable but consumed by nothing.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:22:- React scope: persist `react.*` (and `connection.*`) values to localStorage under a single key; `ConfigService.init` merges stored values over defaults; `saveDraft` writes them back.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:23:- Desktop scope: replace env-only config with `electron-store` persistence (the store already exists for theme). Preload exposes `getDesktopConfig`/`setDesktopConfig`; `saveDraft` pushes desktop values through the bridge. Env vars remain as initial defaults on first run.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:24:- Make desktop config the single source of truth for supported agent commands. The Electron action runner and conversation continuation resolve the same stored value; React never constructs the executable command.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:25:- Wire up or remove the dead entries: `react.showStartupSplash` gates the `StartupSplash` rendering in `app.tsx`; `connection.githubScopes` feeds `readGithubAuthConfig`'s scopes (env value stays the fail-fast fallback) — or drop both entries if not wanted.\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:31:- Every entry shown on `/config` demonstrably affects behavior (or has been removed).\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:36:- `design\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md`\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\F_031_config_persistence.md:37:- `design\\\\\\\\architecture\\\\\\\\initial description\\\\\\\\config.md`\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\file_tree.test.ts:105:    it('marks configured top-level folders as special', () => {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\external_card_import_service.ts:3:import type { CardTypeConfig, MarkdownFile, MoveFile } from '../../data/data_types'\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\external_card_import_service.ts:15:function getFeatureCardType(cardTypes: CardTypeConfig[]) {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\external_card_import_service.ts:17:    if (!cardType) throw new Error(`Missing card type config: ${DEFAULT_CARD_TYPE}`)\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\external_card_import_service.ts:78:    cardTypes: CardTypeConfig[],\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:3:import { configService } from '../config/config_service'\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:24:        configService.clear()\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:29:        configService.init()\\\\r\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:46:        configService.init()\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:70:        configService.init()\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:92:        configService.init()\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\\\\data_service.test.ts:108:    it('coalesces every action text category and pushes once per configured batch interval', async () => {\\\\napp\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\data\\\\\